summary:
  The last device refusing the stream leaves the widget saying it casts.

history:
  "Casting" was raised when the play command went out and never taken
  down by an answer. A Ruark R5se refused two stations (UPnP 716,
  2026-11-11): the footer read "Casting to Ruark R5se" over a silent room
  for more than four minutes, the big button offered Stop, and the volume
  went on being sent to a device that played nothing. When no device is
  left playing or being asked, the cast is over, and the refusal's name
  stands in the footer until the next try.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
          if (!castAns.carried) { root._castFailedName = root.isPlaying() ? "" : castWho; root._castFailedRefused = castNo; root._castEnd(); }

replace:
          if (!castAns.carried) { root._castFailedName = root.isPlaying() ? "" : castWho; root._castFailedRefused = castNo; }

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_a_device_that_refused_the_stream_is_not_cast_to.
  Line-neutral.
